From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chuanchuan <example@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 07:00:54 +0800
Subject: fix: allow UA override when main frame is remote

When the top-level frame is a WebRemoteFrame (typical in OOPIF
renderer processes), ShouldUseUserAgentOverride() previously returned
false because DocumentLoader/DocumentState are unavailable. That caused
cross-origin iframes to ignore RendererPreferences.user_agent_override
set by Electron webContents.setUserAgent().

Return true in that case so OOPIF frames use the synced custom UA.

Related: https://crbug.com/426555
Electron issues: https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/40374
https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/40990
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

diff --git a/content/renderer/render_frame_impl.cc b/content/renderer/render_frame_impl.cc
index 93016ac2f07a76112a407eade082e439f65d4d6d..581399001d56dbca9ef0dbe88ff0d61920294c76 100644
--- a/content/renderer/render_frame_impl.cc
+++ b/content/renderer/render_frame_impl.cc
@@ -4873,7 +4873,7 @@ bool RenderFrameImpl::ShouldUseUserAgentOverride() const {
   // Temporarily return early and fix properly as part of
   // https://crbug.com/426555.
   if (web_view->MainFrame()->IsWebRemoteFrame())
-    return false;
+    return true;
   const WebLocalFrame* main_frame = web_view->MainFrame()->ToWebLocalFrame();
 
   WebDocumentLoader* document_loader = main_frame->GetDocumentLoader();
